Advanced Configuration
Subtask 3.6: Configure Token Synchronization
Set up token synchronization for better user experience.

# Configure token sync window
ipa otpconfig-mod --totp-sync-window=10

# Allow token resynchronization
ipa otpconfig-mod --hotp-sync-window=100

# View current OTP configuration
ipa otpconfig-show
Subtask 3.7: Set Up Backup Tokens
Create backup tokens for users in case their primary device is unavailable.

# Create backup token for testuser1
ipa otptoken-add --owner=testuser1 --desc="TestUser1 Backup Token" --type=hotp

# Generate backup codes (static tokens)
for i in {1..5}; do
    ipa otptoken-add --owner=testuser1 --desc="Backup Code $i" --type=hotp
done

# List all tokens for user
ipa otptoken-find --owner=testuser1
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: OTP Token Not Working
# Check token status
ipa otptoken-find --owner=testuser1

# Verify time synchronization
sudo chrony sources -v

# Check OTP configuration
ipa otpconfig-show

# Reset token if needed
ipa otptoken-mod TOKEN_UUID --disabled=False
Issue 2: SSH Authentication Failing
# Check SSH configuration
sudo sshd -T | grep -i challenge

# Verify PAM configuration
sudo cat /etc/pam.d/sshd | grep -i otp

# Check SSH logs
sudo journalctl -u sshd -f
Issue 3: Time Synchronization Issues
# Check system time
timedatectl status

# Synchronize time
sudo chrony makestep

# Verify NTP synchronization
chrony sources
