Why This Matters
Two-factor authentication is crucial in modern cybersecurity because:

Enhanced Security: Significantly reduces the risk of unauthorized access even if passwords are compromised
Compliance Requirements: Many security frameworks and regulations require multi-factor authentication
User Trust: Demonstrates organizational commitment to protecting sensitive data and systems
Risk Mitigation: Provides an additional security layer against various attack vectors including phishing and credential theft
